  "definition": "Headlight Aim",
  "effectiveDate": "2016-01-06",
  "historyNote": "(See Revision Notes at Chapter Heading Saf-C 3200) #8915, eff 6-22-07, EXPIRED: 6-22-15 New. #10886, INTERIM, eff 7-16-15, EXPIRES: 1-12-16; ss by #11016, eff 1-6-16",
  "inScheme": "https://granitestate.github.io/rules/scheme",
  "notation": "Saf-C 3216.01",
  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-c3200.html",
  "prefLabel": "Saf-C 3216.01 Headlight Aim",
  "priorExpiration": "2016-01-12",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 3216.01 Headlight Aim.\n\n(a) A vehicle shall be rejected if:\n\n(1) A commercially manufactured aimer shows the headlight beam is not straight ahead and 2 degrees down; or\n\n(2) A headlight board shows the headlight beam is not straight ahead and less than 2 inches lower than the horizontal center line of the board, measured 25 feet from the headlamps; or\n\n(3) Headlight aim is unachievable due to fogging or glazing of the lens or reflector.\n\nSource. (See Revision Notes at Chapter Heading Saf-C 3200) #8915, eff 6-22-07, EXPIRED: 6-22-15\n\nNew. #10886, INTERIM, eff 7-16-15, EXPIRES: 1-12-16; ss by #11016, eff 1-6-16",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-c3200.html"
